{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465332-gift-of-sky","id":1465332,"title":"Gift of Sky","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-25T14:45:08-07:00","id":1465332,"title":"Gift of Sky","content":"It can be dangerous to go chasing after the dwellers of the firmament between Earth and the void, as confined to the land as the Uratha normally are. Helios especially frowns at even this slight presumption on the part of Luna\u2019s wayward children, but when spirits of feather and mist are brought down or persuaded to bargain with breezy and twinkling <i>gathra</i>, the rewards are all the more delicious for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cunning: Birdcatcher<br /> <br /> Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Dexterity + Athletics + Cunning - Defense<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The werewolf casts a net of Essence against an airborne entity within (Cunning x 10) meters, sending it crashing to the ground and unable to retake flight for the roll\u2019s successes in turns. This Facet works against both prey flying naturally and those lifted aloft by supernatural means.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The prey also suffers the Immobilized Tilt for the Facet\u2019s duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The prey evades capture.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The werewolf leaves himself open to reprisal, lowering his Defense by two until the start of his next turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Glory: Sky Hunter</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive<br /> <br /> The werewolf activates this Facet when shifting into Gauru, Urshul, or Urhan form to take on the aspect of a mighty eagle, mingled with lupine features. (At Primal Urge 1, this causes the transformation to take an additional turn to complete.) In this combined form, she can fly at her normal Speed, and adds her Glory Renown to rolls to dive bomb or take by surprise land-bound prey. This Facet remains active until the Uratha shifts into another form.<br /> <br /> When falling to <i>Basu-Im</i>, the werewolf activates this Facet automatically at no cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Honor: Updraft</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Intelligence + Science + Honor vs Stamina + Primal Urge<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Uratha conjures a gust of thermal wind that can lift land-bound prey off the earth or launch sky-borne ones even higher. The target (which can be of a Size no larger than Honor + 5) is pushed upward, up to a height of (Honor x 5) meters. This Facet lasts for successes rolled in turns, during which time the prey hovers in place and effectively cannot move under their own will, though they can still turn about, apply Defense against attacks, and take other actions as appropriate. Other effects may still be able to push or pull the prey off the updraft, which, baring other variables, will cause them to fall. Prey with the ability to fly retain their mobility, but cannot descend below the height set by this Facet.<br /> <br /> This Facet can be used on willing targets, or on the user himself, in which case the roll is not contested. A werewolf might employ this to set up tactical ambushes or help packmates scale sheer cliffsides. It can also be used against inanimate objects of appropriate Size so long as they aren\u2019t rooted to the ground, though the object in question rolls its own Size for the contesting dicepool.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Uratha chooses to double either the distance or the duration of the Facet\u2019s effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The prey remains where it is.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The werewolf cannot attempt to use this Facet against the prey again in the current scene. Against willing targets, the Uratha instead miscalculates, accidentally causing his packmate to strike another surface or to fall, inflicting three points of bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Purity: Fear No Heights</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Permanent<br /> <br /> The Uratha never suffers bashing damage from falling, and reduces lethal damage from terminal velocity by her Purity Renown. In addition, add the werewolf\u2019s Purity to rolls to jump, climb, balance, fly, or glide.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom: Read the Winds</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> None or 1 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Survival + Wisdom<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>Scrutinizing the sky, the werewolf gains an understanding of how local weather will change within the next (Wisdom Renown) hours. By spending a point of Essence, the Uratha may dictate the outcome of this forecast, adding or removing a single appropriate Environmental Tilt or changing its degree, grade, or severity by up to her Wisdom Renown. This works against supernaturally induced weather, but in such a case forces a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> Unlike the Facets of the Gift of Weather, the meteorological influence of Read the Winds is not instantaneous, instead coming naturally as the sky changes course. This allows the Uratha time to prepare accordingly.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The werewolf gains insight into local weather patterns instead for the next 24 hours and may spend Essence to alter them accordingly.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The sky keeps its secrets to itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Stymied, the Uratha is unable to activate this Facet again for the next 24 hours.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T22:33:58-07:00","id":1465740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1465332-gift-of-sky#post1465332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Glory: Sky Hunter</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive<br /> <br /> The werewolf activates this Facet when shifting into Gauru, Urshul, or Urhan form to take on the aspect of a mighty eagle, mingled with lupine features. (At Primal Urge 1, this causes the transformation to take an additional turn to complete.) In this combined form, she can fly at her normal Speed, and adds her Glory Renown to rolls to dive bomb or take by surprise land-bound prey. This Facet remains active until the Uratha shifts into another form.<br /> <br /> When falling to <i>Basu-Im</i>, the werewolf activates this Facet automatically at no cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew there would be flying Werewolves in here somewhere. Glory is certainly appropriate. I love the idea of a dive-bombing Gauru. Combine this with Predator's Unmatched Pursuit and things become really scary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}